  "TIP SHAPE: x ZYGO 2 whorls x ALL INNER MAX": { pairs: 104, worstMm: 0.0384, note: "RE-RECORDED BY SPINE-CUP-FOLD (the fold limit, docs/bloom-spine-cup-fold-outcome.md): was 4216 / 0.5065 mm. By band, main -> here: u 0 foot 229 -> 0, u 0.3-0.4 221 -> 0, u 0.4-0.5 1175 -> 0, u 0.5-0.6 609 -> 0, u 0.7-0.8 32 -> 0, u 0.8-0.9 258 -> 0, u 0.9-1.0 92 -> 0, u <0.30 1600 -> 104; what remains is the ROOT BLEND alone (u < 0.30, the worst at u 0.02 beside the foot-to-blade seam) — below where the spine law reaches, so not the fold limit's. Before: RE-RECORDED BY THE PETAL EDGE PROFILE at four bead segments, measured by `node tools/bloom-census-sweep.mjs` over all 909 rows under the census #279 fixed: 4584 -> 5128 pairs, 0.5275 -> 0.5375 mm — RE-RECORDED BY THE APEX NIB (the tip law is truncated at the print floor and closed on a rounded nib, so the outline moves on every row whose blade clears that floor): was 5128 pairs / 0.5375 mm" },
