  'LOBES: x curl 360 (over the fiddlehead, declared on main)': { pairs: 1024, worstMm: 0.5517, note: '(IMPROVED since the magnitude gate landed: this entry read 864 / 0.8971 until 2026-09-17, re-measured on main at 7ebfb7f — docs/bloom-xfail-magnitudes.md) (session 42 re-baselined on the branch: 784 on main at the same control set; over "petalSpineCurl max (360)", which reads 1008 pairs / 0.5233 mm) — RE-RECORDED BY THE PETAL EDGE PROFILE at four bead segments, measured by `node tools/bloom-census-sweep.mjs` over all 909 rows under the census #279 fixed: 864 -> 1000 pairs, 0.507 -> 0.4680 mm'  + ' — RE-RECORDED BY THE APEX NIB (the tip law is truncated at the print floor and closed on a rounded nib, so the outline moves on every row whose blade clears that floor): was 1000 pairs / 0.4680 mm' },
  "LOBES: x cup 1.2 (over a fold declared on main — must not gain a new one)": { pairs: 1104, worstMm: 0.1095, note: "Eva's ruling: authored exception, split to issue #285. Not a fold the cup owns. MECHANISM: the nib closes the blade with a circular arc whose ALONG-u radius of curvature falls to 0.216 / 0.178 / 0.638 of t/2 at v -0.111 / -0.333 / -1.000 on the last station, so its offset surface does not exist; the cup clamp bounds the CROSS-SECTION radius (in v) and this is the other principal curvature (in u). The nib puts its last 7 stations inside 0.05 mm of blade, each carrying a +/- 0.6 mm skin offset (main`s own last gaps there are 0.163..0.406 mm). NOT THE CUP: scaling the cup on the nib by 0 / 0.25 / 0.5 / 1 reads 1856 / 1848 / 1896 / 1688 pairs against the unscaled 1056 — non-monotone, and removing the cup ENTIRELY is the worst of them. NOT THE ARC`S ROWS: APEX_ARC_ROWS 6 -> 1 makes every affected row worse. MAIN`S 0 IS A TESSELLATION COINCIDENCE, not health: petalCup max (1.2) alone reads 80 pairs / 0.0239 mm on main at the same sheet, while the lobes alone read 0 on every tree. See https://github.com/evawm898/Portfolio-Site/issues/285 and docs/bloom-apex-nib-outcome.md." },
