/* ===================================================================
   phase39Matrix() — THE 931 ROWS AS THEY STOOD AT 8bb8685, frozen.

   main's head before the APEX NIB. Every petal there finished on a FLAT face
   two print floors across — 1.6000 mm in EXPORT, 0.3000 mm live — whatever
   exponent `petalTipShape` was asked for, because the tip law reaches exactly
   0 at u = 1 and `halfWidthAt` is a `max` against that floor; and
   `petalLength` was the DRAWN length as well as the asked one, because no cap
   truncated the law.

   A PHASE IS OWED because the ROW SET CHANGED: block 40 appends eleven
   `APEX NIB:` rows, taking the live matrix 931 -> 942, and this is the last
   baseline that pins the squared-tip matrix. It is 39 and not 38 because
   phase38 is the VORONOI INFILL's, registered on main by #284 four hours
   before this branch merged main in — the FROZEN_MATRICES census below is
   what would have caught the collision at module load, by name, had the
   number been reused.

   Registered in BOTH `FROZEN_MATRICES` and `FROZEN_BASE_COMMITS`: a matrix
   with no base commit is verified by nothing, and a base commit with no
   matrix is a phase nobody wrote.

   ITS BYTES DO NOT REPRODUCE ON THIS TREE AND ITS DEFINITIONS DO. The nib
   moves the outline on every row whose blade clears the print floor, which is
   nearly all of them; `--verify-frozen phase39` compares row order, labels
   and set lists and is green. That is the class phase17/19/21/23/24 are
   already in.

   A VERBATIM SNAPSHOT of that commit's buildMatrix(); never edit a label
   inside it. Generated from the base worktree's own buildMatrix() rather than
   transcribed.
   =================================================================== */
